"use strict";(self.webpackChunkstapledons_voyage_site=self.webpackChunkstapledons_voyage_site||[]).push([[5177],{5272(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"/2026/10/03/walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1.mdx","title":"Walkable bridge demo: v0.4.0-dev.1","description":"A development build you can download: walk the captain around the bridge under the live","date":"2026-10-03T20:15:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."},{"inline":false,"label":"Art","permalink":"/news/tags/art","description":"Concept and in-game art."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Walkable bridge demo: v0.4.0-dev.1","date":"2026-10-03T20:15","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey","art"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.1","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.1"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Concept art: the captain and the bridge","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge"}},"content":"import DownloadCard from \'@site/src/components/DownloadCard\';\\n\\nA development build you can download: walk the captain around the bridge under the live\\nrelativistic sky, open the galaxy map from the nav console, and fly a journey to \u03b1 Centauri A\\nthrough the bubble. macOS only, Apple Silicon.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n<DownloadCard compact />\\n\\n![The captain on the bridge at 0.99c, under the live relativistic sky](/img/news/bridge-demo-cruise.jpg)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **The walkable bridge** (M4.2, [#102](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/102)): the bridge disc at the top of the spire,\\n  composited with the live sky through the same camera. The captain walks it (**WASD**, **E** to\\n  use) and ages with ship time.\\n- **Navigation from the bridge:** a nav console opens the galaxy map (**M**), built from the real\\n  catalogues: 5,685 stars within 25 pc, companions at their system\'s distance. Commit to \u03b1\\n  Centauri A and watch the boost, the 0.99c cruise, the brake and the arrival.\\n- **The relativistic sky** behind it all: 335k real stars, aberration and Doppler colour, the\\n  naked-eye exposure, and the forward glow of the cosmic background at extreme speed.\\n- **L** opens the log and **K** the codex.\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\n- The forward bubble-wall glow is off; it returns with the next simulation step.\\n- The standalone sky flight (`-- --voyage`) shows a mirrored sky in this build: fixed on main\\n  ([#107](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/107)), in the next build. The view\\n  from the bridge is correct.\\n- The bridge is v1 demo art; the final art is in progress ([concept art](/concept-art)).\\n- Pre-alpha and unsigned; see [Try it](/docs/try-it) for install notes.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.1](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.1) (macOS development build)"},{"id":"/2026/10/03/concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge.md","title":"Concept art: the captain and the bridge","description":"The ship has faces now. The captain is picked, the crew have proposed portraits, and the bridge","date":"2026-10-03T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"Art","permalink":"/news/tags/art","description":"Concept and in-game art."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Concept art: the captain and the bridge","date":"2026-10-03T18:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","art"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Walkable bridge demo: v0.4.0-dev.1","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Planets are coming","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/planets-are-coming"}},"content":"The ship has faces now. The captain is picked, the crew have proposed portraits, and the bridge\\nstands in the engine over the live sky.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![The captain, the Longline Navigator, at 30, 50, 70 and 90](/img/concept/captain-sheet.jpg)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **The captain, the Longline Navigator** ([#98](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/98)): picked from three silhouette\\n  proposals, and drawn front and back at 30, 50, 70 and 90, because the game spans a 100-year\\n  career.\\n- **Crew cast proposals**: one portrait per role, next to the Medic\'s accepted set.\\n- **Bridge v1** ([#97](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/97), demo art): the first real interior, a disc at the top of the\\n  spire inside the sphere ship. The sky behind the railings is not painted; it is the game\'s live\\n  sky, through the same camera, so at 0.99c it crowds forward and turns blue.\\n\\n![Bridge v1 in the engine at rest and at 0.99c](/img/concept/bridge-v1-parallax.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nBridge v1 is demo art. A v2 quality study is done and the final art is being made. Everything is\\non the [concept art](/concept-art) page, labelled with its status."},{"id":"/2026/10/03/planets-are-coming","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/planets-are-coming","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-planets-are-coming.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-planets-are-coming.md","title":"Planets are coming","description":"A new milestone, M5, brings planets, moons and flybys inside a star system, with the same rule as","date":"2026-10-03T16:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"Planets","permalink":"/news/tags/planets","description":"Planets, moons and flybys (M5)."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Planets are coming","date":"2026-10-03T16:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","planets"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Concept art: the captain and the bridge","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge"},"nextItem":{"title":"The ship\'s AI foundation","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/the-ships-ai-foundation"}},"content":"A new milestone, M5, brings planets, moons and flybys inside a star system, with the same rule as\\nthe sky: real data, real physics.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s done\\n\\n- **The design and the sprint plan are approved** ([#84](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/84), [#86](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/86)).\\n- **A new AILANG package, [`sunholo/celestial`](https://github.com/sunholo-data/ailang-packages/tree/main/packages/celestial)\\n  0.1.0**, published with 93 tests: a Kepler solver, JPL planetary ephemerides for 3000 BC to\\n  3000 AD plus moons, IAU reference frames, light-time, gravity, reflectance, and planetary rings.\\n- **`sunholo/relativity` 0.6 and 0.7**: the bubble\'s forward glow, and the aberrated outline of a\\n  nearby sphere, which is what a planet looks like as you pass it near light speed.\\n\\n## What\'s planned\\n\\nStart held above Earth, pick a body on a system map (the Sun, 8 planets, 11 moons, 4 ring\\nsystems), choose to stop or fly by at 0.001c to 0.99c, commit, and ride the leg. The views will be\\nexact: light-time delay, aberration, and the Terrell rotation that makes a passing sphere look\\nturned. At \u03b1 Centauri, the known and candidate planets will show as points only, with a badge\\nsaying how sure the astronomy is. The first step, the Sol and \u03b1 Cen data and the game\'s package\\npins, has merged ([#99](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/99)).\\n\\nSee the [roadmap](/docs/roadmap)."},{"id":"/2026/10/03/the-ships-ai-foundation","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/the-ships-ai-foundation","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-the-ships-ai-foundation.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-the-ships-ai-foundation.mdx","title":"The ship\'s AI foundation","description":"The crew\'s optional AI layer runs end to end, so far on a deterministic test stub: lines with","date":"2026-10-03T15:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"AI","permalink":"/news/tags/ai","description":"The optional crew AI layer."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"The ship\'s AI foundation","date":"2026-10-03T15:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Planets are coming","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/planets-are-coming"},"nextItem":{"title":"A galaxy map from real catalogues","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues"}},"content":"import {ClipFigure} from \'@site/src/components/Clip\';\\n\\nThe crew\'s optional AI layer runs end to end, so far on a deterministic test stub: lines with\\nemotion markers, portraits that change with them, a voice, and a hard cost ceiling.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **Emotion markers** (AI.1\u2013AI.3): a line carries markers like `{loving}`, validated before the\\n  game uses it.\\n- **A service the game never waits on** (AI.4\u2013AI.7): provider routing, a cache, a supervised\\n  background process, and key hygiene: a key never appears on a command line.\\n- **The Medic\'s accepted portraits**, pinned and content-addressed (AI.8).\\n- **Opt-in and capped** (AI.9): live AI stays off until the player adds a key *and* ticks the box.\\n  A ceiling the player sets (US$0.50 by default) stops spending, and automated runs can never go\\n  live.\\n- **The conversation scene** (AI.10a, [#91](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/91)): the portrait cross-fades as each emotion\\n  marker arrives, the subtitles build segment by segment, and the voice plays.\\n\\n<ClipFigure name=\\"medic\\" sound caption=\\"The Medic scene on the stub. Placeholder voice: the stub\'s test tones, not a performance.\\" />\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nNo live model has been called. The first live run (AI.10b) is attended: one real line and a few\\nvoice auditions under a US$1 ceiling. The voice in the clip is a placeholder."},{"id":"/2026/10/03/a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues.md","title":"A galaxy map from real catalogues","description":"The galaxy map now draws from the same star catalogues as the sky, and stars that belong together","date":"2026-10-03T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"Sky","permalink":"/news/tags/sky","description":"The relativistic sky and the star catalogues."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"A galaxy map from real catalogues","date":"2026-10-03T12:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","sky","journey"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"The ship\'s AI foundation","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/the-ships-ai-foundation"},"nextItem":{"title":"The relativistic sky","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/the-relativistic-sky"}},"content":"The galaxy map now draws from the same star catalogues as the sky, and stars that belong together\\nstay together.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **The map on the catalogue tiers** ([#81](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/81)): 5,687 stars within 25 pc, up from 3,802,\\n  with full-precision positions. \u03b1 Centauri A and B are separate stars you can select.\\n- **Companion stars at their system\'s distance** ([#89](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/89)): a companion within 60\u2033 and\\n  2,000 AU of its primary, agreeing in parallax and proper motion, takes the system\'s distance\\n  rather than its own noisier one. That moved 20,524 companions; Sirius B, for one, now sits with\\n  Sirius A at 8.6 ly.\\n\\n![The galaxy map planning a trip to Sirius A, 8.60 ly](/img/news/map-sirius.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nBoth are in the [walkable bridge demo, v0.4.0-dev.1](/news/2026/10/03/walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1)."},{"id":"/2026/10/03/the-relativistic-sky","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/the-relativistic-sky","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-the-relativistic-sky.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-the-relativistic-sky.mdx","title":"The relativistic sky","description":"The sky out of the window is now the real one: 335,157 stars over the Milky Way, exposed for a","date":"2026-10-03T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"Sky","permalink":"/news/tags/sky","description":"The relativistic sky and the star catalogues."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"The relativistic sky","date":"2026-10-03T09:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","sky"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"A galaxy map from real catalogues","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues"},"nextItem":{"title":"v0.3: plan, commit, transit, arrive","permalink":"/news/2026/10/02/v0-3-m2-journey"}},"content":"import {ClipFigure} from \'@site/src/components/Clip\';\\n\\nThe sky out of the window is now the real one: 335,157 stars over the Milky Way, exposed for a\\ndark-adapted human eye, with the cosmic background glowing ahead at extreme speeds.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **Starfield v2** ([#67](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/67)): 335,157 stars from CNS5, Gaia GCNS and Hipparcos,\\n  instanced on the GPU, with float64 positions rebased around the ship.\\n- **The Milky Way** behind them: the NOIRLab panorama with the catalogue\'s own stars removed, so\\n  stars are not counted twice, Doppler shifted texel by texel.\\n- **A naked-eye exposure** ([#75](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/75), [#80](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/80)): stars in lux and the sky in\\n  cd/m\xb2, calibrated so the faintest visible star lands at V 6.9 (Crumey\'s model says 6.897). The\\n  HUD always says how it is exposing; the readability aids are off by default and labelled.\\n- **The forward CMB glow** ([#79](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/79), fixed in [#88](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/88)): above \u03b3 \u2248 150 the 2.7 K\\n  microwave background, blueshifted, shows up dead ahead; at \u03b3 707 it is a 3,853.7 K blackbody.\\n\\n<ClipFigure name=\\"cmb\\" caption=\\"\u03b3 20 to 707 through a 20\xb0 lens: the stars crowd into a shrinking ball, then the forward CMB warms from deep red to near white.\\" />\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nM1\'s acceptance step (M1.5b) is still open: the reference renders at five speeds and the 60 fps\\nbench at 1440p with everything on. See the [roadmap](/docs/roadmap)."},{"id":"/2026/10/02/v0-3-m2-journey","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026/10/02/v0-3-m2-journey","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-02-v0-3-m2-journey.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-02-v0-3-m2-journey.md","title":"v0.3: plan, commit, transit, arrive","description":"The journey core is complete: pick a star, commit, watch both clocks run, and arrive. Once you","date":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"v0.3: plan, commit, transit, arrive","date":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey"],"release_tag":"v0.3.2-m2-journey","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.3.2-m2-journey"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"The relativistic sky","permalink":"/news/2026/10/03/the-relativistic-sky"},"nextItem":{"title":"v0.2.0: a galaxy map with real numbers","permalink":"/news/2026/10/01/v0-2-0-m2-map"}},"content":"The journey core is complete: pick a star, commit, watch both clocks run, and arrive. Once you\\ncommit, there is no going back.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **Commit:** hold for 1.5 s. After that the simulation refuses every cancel, and says so.\\n- **Transit and arrival:** the phase, both clocks, the distance flown and the energy radiated,\\n  live, until you arrive.\\n- **Deterministic replay:** a 10,000-tick session replays byte for byte on the AILANG VM and the\\n  interpreter.\\n- v0.3.1 opens straight onto the galaxy map; v0.3.2 adds trackpad zoom and Retina scaling.\\n\\n![Commit, and you cannot take it back](/img/gallery/map-commit.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nThe interior of the ship, and a journey you live through on board, are the next milestone (M4).\\n\\n**Releases:** [v0.3.0](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.3.0-m2-journey),\\n[v0.3.1](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.3.1-m2-journey),\\n[v0.3.2](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.3.2-m2-journey) (macOS review builds)"},{"id":"/2026/10/01/v0-2-0-m2-map","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026/10/01/v0-2-0-m2-map","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-01-v0-2-0-m2-map.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-01-v0-2-0-m2-map.md","title":"v0.2.0: a galaxy map with real numbers","description":"The game now opens on a 3D map of the nearby stars. Click one and the simulation plans the trip:","date":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"v0.2.0: a galaxy map with real numbers","date":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey"],"release_tag":"v0.2.0-m2-map","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.2.0-m2-map"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"v0.3: plan, commit, transit, arrive","permalink":"/news/2026/10/02/v0-3-m2-journey"},"nextItem":{"title":"v0.1.0: the spike","permalink":"/news/2026/09/27/v0-1-0-m0"}},"content":"The game now opens on a 3D map of the nearby stars. Click one and the simulation plans the trip:\\nyour years against Earth\'s.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- A galaxy map of the nearby-star catalogue: drag to orbit, scroll to zoom, click to plan.\\n- A cruise slider from 0.9c to 0.999999c, spaced evenly in rapidity, 0.99c by default.\\n- Every number on the panel comes straight from the AILANG simulation. \u03b1 Centauri A at 0.99c:\\n  0.6208 years for you, 4.401 for Earth, 1.80 minutes of boost at each end.\\n\\n![The galaxy map planning a trip to \u03b1 Centauri A](/img/gallery/map-plan.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nCommitting to the journey and flying it came in the next build.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.2.0-m2-map](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.2.0-m2-map) (macOS review build)"},{"id":"/2026/09/27/v0-1-0-m0","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026/09/27/v0-1-0-m0","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-09-27-v0-1-0-m0.md","source":"@site/news/2026-09-27-v0-1-0-m0.md","title":"v0.1.0: the spike","description":"The first review build: an AILANG simulation driving a Godot starfield, with relativity that is","date":"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Sky","permalink":"/news/tags/sky","description":"The relativistic sky and the star catalogues."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"v0.1.0: the spike","date":"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","sky"],"release_tag":"v0.1.0-m0","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.1.0-m0"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"v0.2.0: a galaxy map with real numbers","permalink":"/news/2026/10/01/v0-2-0-m2-map"}},"content":"The first review build: an AILANG simulation driving a Godot starfield, with relativity that is\\ntested rather than eyeballed.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- The simulation runs in AILANG as a child process, talking one line of JSON per tick with Godot\\n  (about 50 \xb5s per round trip). It flies the ship at 1 g with exact rapidity kinematics.\\n- The starfield: 3,802 nearby stars (CNS5), each aberrated toward the bow, coloured as a\\n  Doppler-shifted blackbody and beamed brighter ahead.\\n- 27 physics reference checks, and 9 cases where the GPU shader must put a star where the CPU\\n  reference says, to under 0.1 px.\\n\\n![The sky at 0, 0.5, 0.9 and 0.99c, looking forward, starboard and astern](/img/news/m0-contact-sheet.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nNo Milky Way behind the stars, one axis of motion, and star colours from the spectral class\\nonly. All three were fixed in M1.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.1.0-m0](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.1.0-m0) (macOS review build)"}]}}')}}]);